WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:08.510
Fox's first primetime series, Married…with
Children, remains notable for both its risqué

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:13.880
jokes and abrupt cancellation—as well as
delivering the fledgling FOX network a ratings

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:14.880
hit.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.289
Have you wondered what the members of the
lovably low-class Bundy clan have been up

00:00:18.289 --> 00:00:20.150
to since they went off the air?

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:22.320
Here's what they're working on now.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:23.619
Ed O'Neill

00:00:23.619 --> 00:00:29.500
Since finding fame as curmudgeonly shoe salesman
Al Bundy, Ed O’Neill has had a pretty steady

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.500
career.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:33.610
That isn't to say he hasn't suffered through
a few dry spells, though.

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:38.430
O'Neill starred in a number of short-lived,
obscure projects after Married… with Children.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:43.610
Remember John from Cincinnati, Big Apple,
or the 2003 relaunch of Dragnet?

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.110
We don’t either.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:50.410
Things turned around in 2009, when he landed
the role of Jay Pritchett on ABC's award-winning

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:52.040
Modern Family.

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:56.370
Aside from moving him into a higher tax bracket
in both his personal and fictional lives,

00:00:56.370 --> 00:01:01.960
this also means O'Neill gets paid to pretend
Sofia Vergara is his wife—a job most guys

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:03.470
would do for free.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:07.870
O'Neill has also found the time to earn a
black belt in Brazilian jiu jitsu—not bad

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:10.650
for a guy who recently turned 70.

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.050
Katey Sagal

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:17.550
After ditching Peg Bundy's giant red helmet
of hair, Sagal has worked pretty consistently.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:22.640
In addition to a long-running gig as the voice
of Leela on Matt Groening's animated Futurama,

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:25.290
Sagal starred in &nbsp;8 Simple Rules.

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:29.760
She then went on to score a role on a little
show about a group of motorcycle enthusiasts

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.310
called Sons of Anarchy.

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:36.360
Sagal's work as the vicious Anarchy matriarch
Gemma Teller Morrow was a far cry from her

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:41.370
days as Peg; instead of scarfing down bonbons,
she proved she was just as good at kicking

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:42.720
butt and taking names.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:47.570
Of course, the fact that she's Anarchy creator
Kurt Sutter's wife didn't hurt her chances

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:51.530
of nabbing the part, but she definitely made
the most of the opportunity.

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:56.460
Sagal took home a Golden Globe and a Prism
Award for the role, and she only had to kill

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:58.990
a few people to get there.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:00.670
Christina Applegate

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:05.850
As lovable blonde bombshell Kelly Bundy, Applegate
was a fan favorite, but finding another hit

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.610
series hasn’t been easy.

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:13.470
Her first starring sitcom role in NBC's Jesse
lasted only two seasons, and her next TV project,

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:18.000
ABC's Samantha Who?, was canceled after two
seasons as well.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:23.420
Her third shot at post-Married sitcom hit,
Up All Night, was also off the air after,

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:25.450
you guessed it, two seasons.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:30.360
She's continued to work in film, co-starring
in hits like The Sweetest Thing and the Anchorman

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:33.140
movies, but it hasn't improved her television
luck.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:38.890
All that professional turmoil is nothing compared
to the personal battle she faced in 1998,

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:41.599
when Applegate discovered she had breast cancer.

00:02:41.599 --> 00:02:45.840
Luckily, it was found in its early stages,
and after a double mastectomy, she emerged

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.500
cancer free.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.750
David Faustino

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:53.180
Bud Bundy proved to be the height of David
Faustino's acting career.

00:02:53.180 --> 00:02:57.290
While he's worked consistently, most of his
gigs have been one-off appearances, like his

00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:00.050
appearance in Entourage where he plays himself.

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:03.560
On the other hand, his voice acting career
has been more prosperous.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:15.270
He's lent his vocal talents to popular kid-focused
series like Winx Club and The Legend 

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:18.560
of Korra.

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:23.890
But the best thing about Faustino's post-Married…with
Children life, aside from shedding that glorious

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:26.950
mullet, is his ability to stay out of trouble.

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:32.129
Unlike many former child actors, Faustino
hasn't amassed a collection of mug shots.

00:03:32.129 --> 00:03:37.290
He does have one arrest for marijuana possession
in 2007, according to Fox News, but other

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:39.540
than that, Faustino's been an angel.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:43.890
Maybe some of that good karma will pay off
and his rumored Married…with Children spinoff

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:47.980
series will be a hit, unlike previous spin-off
attempts.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:48.980
Amanda Bearse

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:54.160
If it seems like Amanda Bearse, who played
Bundy neighbor Marcy Rhoades-D'arcy, disappeared

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:57.319
from the TV, it's because she pretty much
has.

00:03:57.319 --> 00:04:01.599
Since 2001, she's only appeared in front of
the camera only seven times.

00:04:01.599 --> 00:04:04.659
However, her directing career's taken off.

00:04:04.659 --> 00:04:10.470
She's lent her camera talents to programs
like Dharma &amp; Greg, MADtv, and the Rosie O'Donnell-produced

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.430
The Big Gay Sketch Show.

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:17.489
Off the set, Bearse revealed some real-life
animosity between her and her television adversary

00:04:17.489 --> 00:04:18.780
Ed O'Neill.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:23.690
When she wed Carrie Schenken in 2010, O'Neill
didn't get an invite because Bearse feared

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:26.180
he'd laugh during the ceremony.

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:35.710
After teasing her about her chicken legs for
over a decade, what'd he expect?

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:37.060
Ted McGinley

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:42.370
Known as much for his role on The Love Boat
as his work playing male bimbo Jefferson D'Arcy,

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:54.550
Ted McGinley has worked consistently since
1997 without landing anything permanent.

00:04:54.550 --> 00:05:00.000
His most prominent role came courtesy of Hope
&amp; Faith, which catapulted Kelly Ripa's career...and

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.150
no one else's.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:06.400
In fact, many consider McGinley's series presence
so lackluster that he's been accused of carrying

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:12.240
the “McGinley Curse,” which claims that
adding him to a show guarantees its cancellation.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:16.190
McGinley counters that accusation by pointing
out that many of the shows he's appeared on

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:19.430
lasted for several seasons after he came aboard.

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:24.270
We see your point, McGinley… but please,
don’t audition for Game of Thrones.

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:25.750
David Garrison

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:30.330
Since gaining fame as Steve Rhodes, David
Garrison has continued to work in television

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:33.630
from time to time, post-Married…with Children.

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:38.470
Garrison's made dozens of one-off appearances
on shows like Arliss, The West Wing, and The

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:39.470
Good Wife.

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:43.470
However, his first love has always been the
theater, to which he returned—and it's a

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:45.199
good thing he did.

00:05:45.199 --> 00:05:50.040
In addition to appearing in Broadway productions
of Bells Are Ringing and The Visit, Garrison

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:55.070
was part of the original cast of the hit Wicked,
in which he played the Wizard of Oz… and

00:05:55.070 --> 00:05:58.520
a very weird, off-Broadway Hannibal Lecter.

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:00.009
Michael the dog

00:06:00.009 --> 00:06:05.690
Known to most as Buck, the Bundys' self-preserving
Briard, Michael retired in 1995.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:11.080
As true fans know, Buck was replaced by Lucky,
the Cocker Spaniel possessed by Buck's reincarnated

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:12.080
spirit.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:17.120
Sadly, Michael actually died less than a year
after his final appearance in 1996, so he

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:19.690
didn't get to enjoy retirement for very long.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:22.960
Michael was 92 in dog years when he passed.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:27.350
Even though that's only 13 in human years,
it wouldn't be an exaggeration to say he had

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:38.729
a fuller life than most of us ever will...

00:06:38.729 --> 00:06:39.820
Thanks for watching!

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:43.919
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:06:43.919 --> 00:06:48.080
And leave us a comment to let us know which
TV show casts you’d like to catch up with...

